Pekko accepts authority-form targets even for `GET`. If effective URI resolution rejects an HTTP/1.0 request with no `Host` under default settings, Pekko passes a rendered authority starting with `//`. This branch exports it as `url.path`, including any credentials in the userinfo.

If we can't get the original target here, skip the ambiguous `//` form when there is no later slash or query.

```suggestion
      // Pekko can render an authority as a single segment prefixed with "//".
      if (target.startsWith("//") && target.indexOf('/', 2) < 0 && target.indexOf('?') < 0) {
        return null;
      }
      return target;
